::ENG2_U01_L01_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: During lunch, Maya noticed that many students threw away unopened milk cartons. She suggested placing a clearly labeled donation cooler near the cafeteria exit so unopened items could be saved for students who needed food later. Question: Which choice best paraphrases the passage?{
~A. Maya wanted students to stop buying milk because the cafeteria had too many cartons.#Incorrect. This changes the meaning. The passage says Maya noticed waste and suggested saving unopened items, not removing milk from lunch.
=B. Maya saw unopened food being wasted and suggested a way to save it for students who might need it.#Correct. This keeps the main idea and important details without copying the original wording.
~C. Maya donated all of her lunch because other students forgot to bring food.#Incorrect. The passage does not say Maya donated her own lunch or that students forgot food.
~D. Maya asked the cafeteria to remove milk cartons from lunch because students disliked them.#Incorrect. This adds an idea that is not in the passage. The issue is waste, not student dislike.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: The class aquarium became cloudy after students overfed the fish for several days. The teacher explained that extra food breaks down in the water and can make the tank unhealthy. Question: What is the most accurate paraphrase?{
~A. The teacher wanted students to clean the aquarium because the fish had grown too large.#Incorrect. The passage does not mention fish size or a cleaning request.
~B. Students fed the fish because the aquarium water was already unhealthy.#Incorrect. This reverses the cause and effect. The water became unhealthy because students overfed the fish.
~C. The fish became unhealthy because the teacher forgot to explain how to feed them.#Incorrect. The passage says the teacher explained the problem. It does not say the teacher forgot anything.
=D. Too much fish food made the water cloudy because uneaten food can break down in the tank.#Correct. This accurately restates the cause, effect, and explanation from the passage.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: A local trail reopened after volunteers repaired the wooden bridge and cleared branches from the path. The park manager said the repairs made the trail safer for walkers and cyclists. Question: Which statement paraphrases the passage accurately?{
=A. Volunteers helped reopen a trail by fixing a bridge and removing branches so people could use it more safely.#Correct. This keeps the main idea and includes the important supporting details.
~B. The park manager closed the trail because walkers and cyclists damaged the wooden bridge.#Incorrect. The passage says the trail reopened after repairs. It does not say walkers or cyclists caused damage.
~C. Volunteers built a new park after a bridge was removed from the trail.#Incorrect. This changes the event. Volunteers repaired a bridge and cleared branches; they did not build a new park.
~D. Walkers and cyclists repaired branches because the trail was unsafe for volunteers.#Incorrect. This confuses who acted and why. Volunteers repaired the trail so walkers and cyclists could use it safely.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: Because the school play needed a city scene, the art class painted tall buildings on cardboard panels. The panels could be moved quickly between scenes without changing the stage floor. Question: What is the main idea of the passage?{
~A. The art class painted the stage floor to make it look like a city.#Incorrect. The passage says the class painted cardboard panels, not the stage floor.
~B. The school play was canceled because the city scene was too difficult to build.#Incorrect. The passage does not say the play was canceled.
=C. The art class made movable city panels to help create the setting for the play.#Correct. This captures the main idea and the reason the panels were useful.
~D. The cardboard panels were used because the play did not need a setting.#Incorrect. The passage says the play needed a city scene, so this answer contradicts the text.
}

::ENG2_U01_L01_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage: When the debate team practiced, each speaker had two minutes to present a claim and one piece of evidence. The coach limited the time so students would learn to explain their ideas clearly and briefly. Question: Which paraphrase is most accurate?{
~A. The coach stopped the debate team from using evidence during practice.#Incorrect. The passage says each speaker used one piece of evidence.
=B. The coach used a time limit to help speakers practice making clear, brief arguments with evidence.#Correct. This keeps the main idea and includes the purpose of the time limit.
~C. The debate team practiced for two minutes because the coach did not want students to speak.#Incorrect. The passage says students did speak, but within a time limit.
~D. Each speaker presented two claims because the debate team needed longer speeches.#Incorrect. The passage says each speaker had two minutes, not two claims or longer speeches.
}

